  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 and avgpool (config_005, 0.6501 acc / 0.6275 F1), and for PCA multiprofile avgpool also outperformed transformer (config_002 vs config_003). This leaves uncertainty about whether transformer aggregation could improve the best scvi representation. config_006 changes only aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping the promising scvi_n200 multiprofile setting, so it directly isolates the aggregation effect. Under a limited budget, this is a low-risk, high-information extension of the current best direction before moving to more complex multimodal fusion."
